Bash Notes
Input / Output
-----------------

read -r basically mean raw input. It does not try to interpret things.

read by default reads only the first line.

":" = "true"

Can do ./whileReadInput < file.txt
This eliminates the use of using cat unneedingly.

These are also both valid:
<file.txt ./whileReadInput
< file.txt ./whileReadInput

$# is the amount of arguments given

exit breaks out of a script
